WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.170
- So, we were just
talking about giving back.

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:03.800
So you actually did,

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.000
was it a "Designing Women"
table read for charity?

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.580
Is that what I... that's amazing!

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.640
- We actually got together last year

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.930
and we read the pilot script.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.114
- How fun was that?
- Yeah.

00:00:13.114 --> 00:00:16.291
- From thirty five years ago,

00:00:16.291 --> 00:00:17.124
something like that. (laughing)

00:00:17.124 --> 00:00:18.400
- Yeah, that's crazy.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.708
- And it was weird cause it
felt like we had just done it.

00:00:20.708 --> 00:00:21.541
- [Kelly] Oh, really?

00:00:21.541 --> 00:00:22.680
- And I could hear everybody's...

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.110
I could just hear everybody in my head

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:25.700
and how it used to be 'cause,

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.455
unfortunately, of course,
we didn't have um...

00:00:27.455 --> 00:00:28.490
- [Kelly] Didn't have Dixie.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:31.800
- [Jean] Dixie, and Delta
couldn't do it, so we, you know.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.280
But it was just like we
had just been doing it.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.180
It was crazy.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.950
- Is there an episode
from "Designing Women"

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.414
that still kind of sticks out for you?

00:00:39.414 --> 00:00:41.010
I have so many!

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.224
- Oh gosh, there was five years of them.

00:00:43.224 --> 00:00:45.550
- Do you wanna know mine? Fine.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:46.870
- Yeah, I'm dying to know
what your favorite is!

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:49.920
- Mine is when y'all were snowed in!

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.427
- Oh, "Reservations for Eight"
- And the guys and the girls,

00:00:51.427 --> 00:00:52.260
were...

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:53.093
Yeah.

00:00:53.093 --> 00:00:54.684
- Yeah, so we all got in a
- I loved that one.

00:00:54.684 --> 00:00:55.517
big fights, the women against the men.

00:00:55.517 --> 00:00:56.680
- I know, cause I love it.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:57.513
- Yeah.

00:00:57.513 --> 00:00:58.870
- And of course the one
where I met my husband,

00:00:58.870 --> 00:00:59.703
of course stands out.

00:00:59.703 --> 00:01:01.680
That was the fifth episode of the season.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:02.604
We hadn't even aired yet.

00:01:02.604 --> 00:01:03.437
- [Kelly] Oh, wow.

00:01:03.437 --> 00:01:04.270
- The show had never aired

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:06.170
and we were shooting episode number five

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:07.950
and he'd played Annie's boyfriend.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:10.200
- Did you know right
away when you first met?

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:13.140
- We were never apart
after that day. (laughing)

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.062
- [Audience] Aww.
- Oh my gosh, really?

00:01:15.062 --> 00:01:15.895
- Yeah.

00:01:15.895 --> 00:01:17.090
I don't mean we moved in
together the next day.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:17.944
I don't mean that!

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:18.777
(audience and Kelly laughing)

00:01:18.777 --> 00:01:19.610
Don't mean that.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:20.863
- This is happening.
- No, and he...

00:01:20.863 --> 00:01:23.900
he invited me to come and
see a play that he was doing.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.190
Of course I went 17 times.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:26.590
(Kelly awing)

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:28.210
And then, you know, we lived
about 15 minutes apart,

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:29.420
but we would talk every night on the phone

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:30.633
for about two hours.

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:32.810
- I love that!

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:33.953
That's rare!

